The playbooks under engine/docket/skills/recon/ and engine/docket/skills/triage/
are DERIVED from strix's vulnerability skills (strix/skills/vulnerabilities/*.md).

Changes made:
  - Each source file was split into two, by consumer rather than by vulnerability:
    a "recon" playbook (Attack Surface, Key Vulnerabilities, High-Value Targets,
    Special Contexts) and a "triage" playbook (False Positives, Impact).
  - Sections describing procedure against a live target were REMOVED: Testing
    Methodology, Validation, Bypass Techniques, active Reconnaissance, Advanced
    Techniques, Chaining Attacks, Pro Tips, Summary. docket's recon and triage
    agents read source and execute nothing, so those instructions do not apply to
    them.
  - Section headings were renamed to the question the agent is answering
    ("False Positives" -> "Not a bug when").
  - A docket-authored header was prepended to each file, framing the content for
    an agent that reads source rather than one that sends requests.
  - The retained text is otherwise unmodified.

The derivation is performed by scripts/build_skills.py and can be re-run or
verified with `python scripts/build_skills.py --check`.
